What is RAG?

Imagine you have an LLM like ChatGPT.

You ask:

"What is the leave policy in my  employee handbook?"

The LLM doesn't know, because:

That handbook is not part of its training data.
It cannot magically read files on your computer.
It may guess or hallucinate.

RAG solves this problem.

Instead of relying only on what the LLM already knows, we first retrieve relevant information from your own documents and then provide that information to the LLM before it generates an answer.

Simple Pipeline
User Question
      │
      ▼
Retrieve relevant documents
      │
      ▼
Attach retrieved context
      │
      ▼
LLM generates answer
      │
      ▼
Answer grounded in your documents

So the LLM is no longer answering from memory alone—it is answering using your data.

